COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff. The
            reference sequence was derived from AL671762.10.
            This sequence is a reference standard in the RefSeqGene project.
            
            Summary: This gene encodes a 70kDa heat shock protein. In
            conjunction with other heat shock proteins, this protein stabilizes
            existing proteins against aggregation and mediates the folding of
            newly translated proteins in the cytosol and in organelles. The
            gene is located in the major histocompatibility complex class III
            region, in a cluster with two closely related genes which also
            encode isoforms of the 70kDa heat shock protein. [provided by
            RefSeq, Jul 2008].
